<h2 id="summary" data-toc-name="Summary">Summary</h2><p>Alright's audience watched iPop Star 2026 but had no reason to return daily or to pay. I designed a daily voting loop where fans back a favourite mentor, win prizes and see their impact on a live leaderboard. An optional membership multiplier lets fans give their mentor extra votes, which tied revenue to something fans already cared about.</p>


<div class="callout-block">
  <h3>My contribution: </h3>
  <div class="callout-content">
I framed the problem with product and business leads, set the monetization guardrails (free vote stays free, no pay-to-win feel), designed the end-to-end experience, and ran testing and a staged rollout with data.
  </div>
</div>

<h2 id="context" data-toc-name="Context">Context</h2><div><p>Alright is an entertainment app with 5M+ users. iPop Star 2026 was a flagship music show and the company's biggest moment of the year for acquisition. Leadership wanted two outcomes from one feature: <b>grow the app</b> and <b>grow revenue</b>.</p></div>


<div class="cards-grid cards-grid-2">
  <div class="card">
    <h3 style="font-size:18px">Constraints</h3>
    <p>Fixed show calendar, live-night traffic spikes, a short build window and a need to keep the free experience fair.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3 style="font-size:18px">Stakeholders</h3>
    <p>Product, Engineering, Data, Marketing, the show's content team and Finance.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 id="problem-framing" data-toc-name="Problem Framing">Problem framing</h2><div>The brief was "add voting." I reframed it, because voting alone does not create growth or revenue. The real problems were behavioural and commercial.</div>


<div class="cards-grid cards-grid-3">
  <div class="card">
    <h3 style="font-size:18px">User</h3>
    <p>Fans watch passively and cannot show support for their favourite mentor.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3 style="font-size:18px">Behaviour</h3>
    <p>No daily trigger, so viewers leave after each episode.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3 style="font-size:18px">Business</h3>
    <p>Low upgrade intent. Membership offered no value tied to the show.</p>
  </div>
</div>


<div class="callout-block">
  <h3>How might we</h3>
  <div class="callout-content">
Make supporting a mentor a daily habit, and make upgrading feel like a natural way to support them more?
  </div>
</div>

<h2 id="my-role" data-toc-name="My Role">My role and ownership<br></h2><div><ul><li><b>Led design</b> across voting, leaderboard, rewards and membership, working with one other designer on UI.</li><li><b>Shaped the roadmap</b> with the PM: what ships for the first live episode and what follows.</li><li><b>Set monetization principles</b> and aligned Finance, Marketing and Engineering on them.</li><li><b>Defined success metrics</b> and the experiment plan with Data.</li><li><b>Handed off</b> specs, states and components to Engineering, and stayed in QA through launch.</li></ul></div>
